    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0276" n="226" xml:id="pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/344</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Harbin</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moser</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-26T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Stevens:</p>
                <p>Ambassador Francis has asked you to send six units of Railway Service Corps to
                    European Russia. Take no action at present. What progress are you making at
                    Harbin? Are any of the men still at Nagasaki? Glad you are continuing
                    efforts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
